# Per-run tool-call logs. Kept out of the repository for two reasons: they record
# commands issued against a private checkout, symbol names and all, and they carry
# absolute paths from whatever machine produced them. RESULTS.md states the numbers and
# how to reproduce them; the raw logs stay local.
runs/

# Machine-specific scaffolding: a wrapper pointing at an extracted binary.
armbin/

# `arms/cairn_full.md` used to be ignored here, as "the arm prompt assembled from a
# preamble plus SKILL.md at run time". Nothing performed that assembly, so the file was
# written by hand once and then sat going stale while the guide grew - the backend arm
# spent several rounds handing out advice the tool had stopped giving. Both halves of that
# are fixed: `build-arms.sh` does the assembling, and the arms are tracked so CI can check
# they match `skill/SKILL.md`. A file nobody can see is a file nobody notices is wrong.

# Byte-compiled harness modules, produced whenever stress.py is imported rather than run.
__pycache__/
